  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Frontend and API",
      "items": [
        "LandingPage.tsx supplies the public page; App.tsx owns dashboard, upload, analysis, misconception, intervention and results screens.",
        "api/client.ts sends multipart files and typed JSON. ApiStatus.tsx probes /health. localStorage contains IDs; API GETs restore durable records.",
        "FastAPI registers five route modules; Pydantic schemas validate request/response structures. Browser access uses configured CORS; user authentication is not implemented."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Detection and retrieval",
      "items": [
        "CSV correctness is the supplied is_correct boolean, not AI grading. Only answered incorrect responses enter question-specific complete-link cosine grouping.",
        "Defaults: similarity 0.70, support at least 3. Groups retain exact representative answers, membership and coherence; labels remain generic and provisional.",
        "UTF-8 .txt material only: normalization, 900-character chunks with 120-character overlap, local embeddings, top 3 retrieval hits above 0.42. Cache rebuilds on first retrieval after restart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Generation and approval",
      "items": [
        "grounded_remediation_v1 packages selected group evidence and retrieved passages. Default configured model: gemini-3.1-flash-lite.",
        "Gemini returns JSON; schema, content and referenced chunk IDs are checked before saving. Missing context and provider failure produce no draft.",
        "Teacher PATCH saves edits or explicitly approves/rejects. Approved/rejected records are terminal; follow-up comparison requires approval."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Persistence and comparison",
      "items": [
        "Postgres adapters own actual SQL I/O. Psycopg pool has max size 5 and prepared statements disabled for transaction-pooler compatibility.",
        "Tables: assessments, questions, student_responses, analysis_runs, misconception_groups, misconception_members, learning_materials, document_chunks, interventions, intervention_sources, assessment_comparisons.",
        "Follow-up uses the same parser and detector, validates context, matches the same question with at least 2 overlapping group members, and stores observed before/after metrics without claiming causation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Repository and operations",
      "items": [
        "Source references pin commit 5fb327fd05973018c5dc3debb5c5dc826ccddd82. Existing uncommitted changes: STATUS.md, TASKS.md, SESSION_PROGRESS.md, backend/.env.example, frontend/src/App.tsx and WorkspacePolish.css.",
        "data/demo supplies explicitly synthetic baseline/follow-up CSVs and teaching notes through ordinary parser/model paths; mockData.ts supplies UI scenario/navigation metadata.",
        "scripts/demo.sh manages local Vite/Uvicorn processes, configuration and health. backend/tests covers validation, AI failures, grounding, persistence and results; PostgreSQL integration is opt-in.",
        "Current documentation reports Vercel frontend and Render backend; hosted browser golden-path verification remains pending. Hosting is reported context, not a source-configured deployment boundary."
      ]
    }
  ]
